From 4e8e11af697749cf5bfdd606d34510156004691e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Sutter <phil@nwl.cc>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 01:45:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mips: dts: Add rb4xx DTS

Copied from openwrt HEAD at c9406df91836b5c94a395b61ebe5c16e08e2c779
plus the following fixes:

* Add missing data to rb4xx nand definition

Engine type should not be necessary since rawnand_dt_init() sets
chip->ecc.engine_type only if the DTB specified it and nand_rb4xx sets
it correctly. Define it anyway for the sake of completeness.

* Set rb493g MMC voltage ranges

The old platform device in mach-rb4xx.c had an ocr_mask of
'MMC_VDD_32_33 | MMC_VDD_33_34', this looks like the correct equivalent.

* Drop fixed rb4xx-gpio base

Effectively convert the device to dynamic base allocation this way,
eliminating the warning about deprecated static allocation. All this is
not relevant anyway since rb4xx-gpio merely cares about the offset and
passes it on to rb4xx-cpld (spi) driver.

Signed-off-by: Phil Sutter <phil@nwl.cc>
